Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:47:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Refactor workout handlers with role-based access, FSM
 improvements, and exercise parameter configuration

- Added `check_workout_access` and `can_access_workout` functions to enforce strict role-based permissions (admin, trainer, player) for viewing workouts
- Implemented robust FSM states for creating workouts: `CreateWorkoutStates` now handles name/description input, block selection, and manual/exercise search flows
- Enhanced exercise addition logic with support for manual text entry, database-backed exercises, and configurable parameters (sets, reps, %1RM, rest)
- Integrated 1RM test workflow: prompts users to take a test if 1RM data is missing when specifying percentage-based loads
- Added quick-add buttons for default exercise parameters and streamlined navigation between blocks and exercise lists
- Improved error handling and logging in all callback and message handlers to ensure stable bot operation during complex interactions
